# Cluster credentials — these must NEVER enter the repository. A kubeconfig used
# for local development carries the client certificate and key of a real
# cluster, and a single `git add -A` would commit it. The rule lives here, not in
# the developer's attention.
kube-configs/
*.kubeconfig
